  <article class="tp-article">

  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> the U.S. National Academies set total water at about <strong>3.7&nbsp;L (125&nbsp;oz) a day for men</strong> and <strong>2.7&nbsp;L (91&nbsp;oz) for women</strong>, including water from food. From drinks, that is roughly <strong>11&ndash;15 cups</strong> for men and <strong>8&ndash;11 cups</strong> for women, plus more when you exercise or it is hot.</p></div>

